<title>POLAND: Dlr/zloty seen down at 3.07 in Sept '97 - fin min.</title>
<headline>Dlr/zloty seen down at 3.07 in Sept '97 - fin min.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish currency is likely to weaken against the dollar to 3.07 zlotys in September 1997 from 2.80 zlotys on Friday, Finance Minister Grzegorz Kolodko told the private Radio Zet in an interview.</p>
<p>A recent Reuter poll of the country's 26 top banks showed dealers expected the dollar/zloty exchange rate 12 months ahead, in September 1997, at 3.04 zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
